# orditect-protocol

**Storage interaction contracts for the Orditect ecosystem**

[![Python 3.12+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.12+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)

`orditect-protocol` defines the narrow protocols (interfaces) and data models
that decouple the Orditect frameworks (`orditect-core` / `orditect-flow` /
`orditect-stream`) from concrete storage backends.

## Scope

**In scope:**
- Contract definitions (Protocols) for four storage domains:
  Content / Audit / Result / Snapshot.
- Shared data models (TaskPointer, TaskSnapshot, AuditEvent, ...).
- Conformance test kit (verifies any backend implementation honors the contracts).

**Out of scope:**
- No storage implementation (this package is contract-only).
- No governance hot path (semaphore / quota / task state stays in
  `orditect-core`, pinned to Redis).
- No business query semantics (no WHERE-style DSL; mechanism fields only).

## Layout

- `orditect.protocol.models` — data models (B2)
- `orditect.protocol.domains` — storage domain protocols (B4-B6)
- `orditect.protocol.conformance` — conformance test kit (B7)
- `docs/terms.md` — consistency terms (B3)

## Status

v0.1.0 (B0 skeleton). Contracts are being bootstrapped; see CHANGELOG.
